 "_doc": "V\u00e4in\u00e4m\u00f6inen (GAME_DESIGN.md: Heroes; art 10/31/2026). Built by tools/art/build_vainamoinen.py on the shared body in tools/art/hero_kit.py; rules in docs/ART_RULES.md. From the Kalevala (Elias L\u00f6nnrot, 1835/1849), where he is 'old and steadfast V\u00e4in\u00e4m\u00f6inen', the eternal singer: an old man with long white hair and a long white beard, in a plain wool coat with a woven belt, and leather boots. He carries his kantele (Kalevala runos 40 and 44: he makes the first kantele from a great pike's jawbone, then one of birch), drawn separately as the picture for his Runo Song (data/art/weapons/runo_song.json).",
